## Blocking finding

Commit 5c29c1a65bcf084c8ad27d91bcaf9d319f6146f3 is signed. Its raw commit object contains a gpgsig SSH signature header, and git verifies it as a good signature with ECDSA key fingerprint SHA256:V6JiKG7J29mjsvikcLoSVp0bLa77VTsFy12gnLO81cM. Repository configuration resolves commit.gpgsign=true from /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/curator-spec/.git/config and gpg.format=ssh from the user config, so the plain git commit command auto-signed it. This contradicts both the explicit no-signing task boundary and the developer handoff claim that no signing occurred. The exact commit therefore cannot be accepted or pushed.

